{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["Seed of a blameless man, El deliver him, and by the hand of His servant the decree of His knowledge — behold, the commandment of the month, it is the sod of the section \"Bo unto Pharaoh\": <b>Bo unto Pharaoh.</b> Go unto him this time, and do not be astonished because his heart was hardened until now, for I have hardened his heart and the heart of his servants. He mentioned the heart of his servants because their heart was weakened when the plague of the locusts came:" "And the meaning of \"I have hardened his heart,\" in order that I set these My signs in his midst — and the opinion of the sages of Sepharad is not unanimous, for some say that שתי is like בינו, שימו, and similar forms, and likewise ישית, ישים, יבין, and similar forms in all the signs, and some say that it is from the binyan of the hiphil, and it is the binyanḥaser, because they found או מי ישום אלם (above 4:11), לשוש עליך לטוב כאשר שש על אבותיך (Deuteronomy 30:9) which is from the binyan of the kal, and some say ישיש like ישוש, and שיתי like שומי, and all are from the binyan of the kal:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:08.952230631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}